[1.307919, "o", "23:4. Delivery date selection: the customer must not be able to choose a Sunday,\r\n24-   since Sarah does not deliver on Sundays.\r\n"]
[3.710753, "o", "\r\n\u001b[38;5;108m# Kane's suite reported 4 of 5 tests passing and 0 failed.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[5.013139, "o", "\r\n\u001b[38;5;108m# Signed Off read the same evidence and refused to sign it off.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[6.31558, "o", "\u001b[38;5;108m$\u001b[0m node /home/kiter/kane/packages/cli/bin/signedoff.mjs brief --pack .testmuai/evidence/39691de6-b770-4388-8467-e94b1ef74004.evidence\r\n"]
[6.670958, "o", "2 promises in the signed scope are not proven by the current build.\r\n\r\nSarah Whitmore is waiting to accept or reject this milestone.\r\n\r\nFix the product code so each promise below holds. Do not change the tests, and do\r\nnot change the scope document — both are the record of what was agreed.\r\n\r\n## 1. After a visitor attempts to choose Sunday during guest checkout, Sunday is not shown as the selected delivery date.\r\n\r\nFrom this part of the signed scope: \"3. A visitor can complete checkout as a guest — we agreed no account is required, because Sarah's customers are mostly one-off buyers.\"\r\n\r\nWhy it is not proven: The run recorded the calendar state as “Sunday 23 August”, but this was promised not to happen.\r\n\r\nWhat the browser observed:\r\n  - whether the delivery date control exposes a Sunday date option: true\r\n  - the saved value of the delivery-date field: 2026-08-23\r\n  - the calendar control state after the Sunday selection attempt: {\"selectedText\":\"Sunday 23 August\",\"selectedValue\":\"2026-08-23\",\"sundayOptions\":[\"Sunday 23 August\",\"Sunday 30 August\",\"Sunday 6 September\"],\"ariaInvalid\":\"false\"}\r\n  - the inline validation message shown for the delivery-date field: We deliver Monday to Saturday. Sundays are not available.\r\n  - whether Sunday is shown as the selected delivery date in the delivery date field: false\r\n  - Assertion check: {'status': 'passed', 'composite_operator': 'and', 'sub_results': [{'description': 'After a visitor attempts to choose Sunday during guest checkout, Sunday is not shown as the selected delivery date.', 'passed': True, 'operator': 'equals', 'transforms': ['strip'], 'expected': 'false', 'extracted_value': 'false'}]}\r\n\r\n## 2. Sunday is not selectable as a delivery date.\r\n\r\nFrom this part of the signed scope: \"3. A visitor can complete checkout as a guest — we agreed no account is required, because Sarah's customers are mostly one-off buyers.\"\r\n\r\nWhy it is not proven: The run recorded the calendar state as “Sunday 23 August”, but this was promised not to happen.\r\n\r\nWhat the browser observed:\r\n  - whether the delivery date control exposes a Sunday date option: true\r\n  - the saved value of the delivery-date field: 2026-08-23\r\n  - the calendar control state after the Sunday selection attempt: {\"selectedText\":\"Sunday 23 August\",\"selectedValue\":\"2026-08-23\",\"sundayOptions\":[\"Sunday 23 August\",\"Sunday 30 August\",\"Sunday 6 September\"],\"ariaInvalid\":\"false\"}\r\n  - the inline validation message shown for the delivery-date field: We deliver Monday to Saturday. Sundays are not available.\r\n  - whether Sunday is shown as the selected delivery date in the delivery date field: false\r\n  - Assertion check: {'status': 'passed', 'composite_operator': 'and', 'sub_results': [{'description': 'After a visitor attempts to choose Sunday during guest checkout, Sunday is not shown as the selected delivery date.', 'passed': True, 'operator': 'equals', 'transforms': ['strip'], 'expected': 'false', 'extracted_value': 'false'}]}\r\n\r\nWhen you have made the change, re-run:\r\n\r\n    signedoff verify --url <url>\r\n\r\nSteps that already passed replay from cache, so re-checking is fast and free.\r\n"]
